\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 DATASET: PSPLIB\

\f1\b0 (Last update: January 2024)\
\

\f0\b Paper\

\f1\b0 This dataset has been presented in the following paper:\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Kolisch, R. and Sprecher, A. (1996). PSPLIB - A project scheduling problem library. European Journal of Operational Research, 96:205-216\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
Please use these references when referring to this dataset.
\f0\b \
\
Problem\
\

\f1\b0 PSPLIB is the most widely used dataset in the project scheduling literature for the resource-constrained project scheduling problem.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}The instances are \ul not\ulnone  in the Patterson format (but instead, in the original format presented in the paper mentioned above).\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}If you prefer to download them in the Patterson format, they are available in the ALL folder (in four versions, as discussed in the folder).\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

